  <img decoding="async" width="768" height="432" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/bank-of-america-768x432-1.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-post-image" alt="Bank of America Establishes Cryptocurrency Research Team" loading="lazy" style="float:left; margin:0 15px 15px 0;" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/bank-of-america-768x432-1.jpg 768w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/bank-of-america-300x169.jpg 300w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/bank-of-america-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/bank-of-america-696x385.jpg 696w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/bank-of-america-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/bank-of-america-747x420.jpg 747w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/bank-of-america-190x107.jpg 190w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/bank-of-america-380x214.jpg 380w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/bank-of-america-760x428.jpg 760w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/bank-of-america.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px" /></p> 
  
  <p>
    <strong>Bank of America has become the latest major bank to make a foray into the cryptocurrency sector. According to an internal memo, the bank has created a team dedicated to researching cryptocurrencies. Bank of America believes that it is “uniquely positioned to provide thought leadership” on cryptocurrencies and the technology behind them.</strong>
  </p>
  
  <ul>
    <li>
      Bank of America (BOFA) has created a new team dedicated to researching cryptocurrencies, according to an internal memo seen by Bloomberg. A spokeswoman for the bank confirmed the contents of the memo.
    </li>
    <li>
      The new crypto team will be led by Alkesh Shah, a founding member of the Data & Innovation Strategy Group at Bank of America. It will report to Michael Maras, who leads the bank’s global fixed income, currencies, and commodities research. Besides cryptocurrencies, the team will also cover technologies tied to digital currencies.
    </li>
    <li>
      Candace Browning, head of Bank of America’s global research, said in the memo:
    </li>
  </ul>
  
  <blockquote>
    <p>
      Cryptocurrencies and digital assets constitute one of the fastest growing emerging technology ecosystems. We are uniquely positioned to provide thought leadership due to our strong industry research analysis, market-leading global payments platform and our blockchain expertise.
    </p>
  </blockquote>
  
  <ul>
    <li>
      A growing number of investment banks have begun offering or are in the process of offering cryptocurrency services to their clients. They include Goldman Sachs, Morgan Stanley, Citigroup, Standard Chartered, Wells Fargo, and DBS.
    </li>
  </ul>
  
  <p>
    <em><strong>What do you think about Bank of America launching a dedicated crypto research team? Let us know in the comments section below.</strong></em>
  </p>
